KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ auto-return pack call yields 3: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [dcl.spec.auto]/3-4 + [temp.variadic]/4-5.  A function template
with a DEDUCED return type (`auto` / `decltype(auto)`) whose body returns a call
containing a pack expansion (`decltype(auto) impl(seq<I...>){ return add(I...); }`)
is left incomplete by the C++ front-end ("C++ front-end could not fully
type-check 'main' (unsupported construct); its body is left incomplete").  The
call is never really evaluated, so BOTH assertions are skipped and CBMC reports
VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL vacuously -- which does NOT match the desc above, so this
correctly registers as a known bug.  When the deduced return type is supported,
the body is checked, assertion 2 ("WRONG must FAIL") fails, and the desc matches
(promote to CORE).

A TRAILING return type over the same pack call (`-> decltype(add(I...))`) IS
handled correctly (cpp11_decltype_return_nontype_pack_call, CORE); the defect is
specific to a DEDUCED return type whose deduction must expand the pack-expansion
call in the return statement.  This is the remaining layer of cpp17_apply_basic
(std::apply and __apply_impl return `decltype(auto)`).  g++ runs r == 3; clang++
accepts.
